From 6df40ea0a097d8c1159833b7711e7c22592aa9fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ProArt P16 Linux <proart-p16-linux@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 02:50:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] soundwire: mediatek: re-apply the pin bias on system
 resume

mtk_sdw_apply_pin_config() programs the bias of the SoundWire pads from
the _CRS PinFunction entries (bus keeper on the data lines, pull-down on
the clock lines) once, at probe. Link 1's pads are not in the always-on
domain - the clock ops hold a VCORE request for that link while it runs
and release it in system suspend - so after a long s2idle in which the
SoC drops every audio vote the bias can come back at its reset default.
Nothing reprograms it afterwards: the links restart with a floating
data line and the peripherals see corrupted frames.

Re-apply the pin configuration in the system resume path before the
links are brought back. A failure only warns, the bias may still be
intact.
---
 drivers/soundwire/mediatek/mtk-sdw.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soundwire/mediatek/mtk-sdw.c b/drivers/soundwire/mediatek/mtk-sdw.c
index a14df48..788258e 100644
--- a/drivers/soundwire/mediatek/mtk-sdw.c
+++ b/drivers/soundwire/mediatek/mtk-sdw.c
@@ -1643,6 +1643,19 @@ static int mtk_sdw_resume(struct device *dev)
 		}
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * The pad bias that probe programs from the _CRS PinFunction entries
+	 * (bus keeper on the data lines, pull-down on the clocks) is not part
+	 * of the always-on state: link 1's pads are outside the AO domain
+	 * (see the VCORE request in the clock ops) and the SoC may power that
+	 * area down once every audio vote is gone in a long s2idle. Nothing
+	 * else reprograms it, so restore it before the links restart. A
+	 * failure is not fatal: the bias may still be intact.
+	 */
+	ret = mtk_sdw_apply_pin_config(dev);
+	if (ret)
+		dev_warn(dev, "re-applying the pin bias failed: %d\n", ret);
+
 	/* 2. restore setting */
 	ret = mtk_sdw_restore_hw_settings(mst);
 	if (ret) {
